{"chapter": "sets", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "05N1", "placeholders": {"EMPHCLOSE_0001": "}", "EMPHCLOSE_0002": "}", "EMPHCLOSE_0003": "}", "EMPHOPEN_0001": "\\emph{", "EMPHOPEN_0002": "\\emph{", "EMPHOPEN_0003": "\\emph{", "MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$x\\in T$", "MATH_0003": "$x\\subset T$", "MATH_0004": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0005": "$\\in$", "MATH_0006": "$\\alpha + 1 = \\alpha \\cup \\{\\alpha\\}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\alpha$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\noindent\n", "suffix": " "}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:da8d19d711871b8b49fbce790d519f8474cabb3e9ff8b72913f3dd13a85e8914", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:52d33729e31b2f886dbe6f73a5046ad3f809ccb36d993377441d3731dab98dff", "source_text": "A set <MATH_0001> is <EMPHOPEN_0001>transitive<EMPHCLOSE_0001> if <MATH_0002> implies <MATH_0003>. A set <MATH_0004> is an <EMPHOPEN_0002>ordinal<EMPHCLOSE_0002> if it is transitive and well-ordered by <MATH_0005>. In this case, we define <MATH_0006>, which is another ordinal called the <EMPHOPEN_0003>successor<EMPHCLOSE_0003> of <MATH_0007>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fdf52c8bd9c4fd7639cb49072843c170c3fe81123b7f7005fe60c663875001bf", "unit_id": "tag:05N1:p001"}
{"chapter": "sets", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "05N1", "placeholders": {"EMPHCLOSE_0001": "}", "EMPHCLOSE_0002": "}", "EMPHOPEN_0001": "\\emph{", "EMPHOPEN_0002": "\\emph{", "MATH_0001": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0002": "$\\beta$", "MATH_0003": "$\\alpha = \\beta + 1$", "MATH_0004": "$\\emptyset$", "MATH_0005": "$0$", "MATH_0006": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0007": "$0$", "MATH_0008": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\alpha\n=\n\\bigcup\\nolimits_{\\gamma \\in \\alpha} \\gamma.\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": " "}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f296cff51c014bbe81ec27064452db68df30469b9293bf3833406e7f18b3dea5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c4f177849442e65f7f3f4ea7acfd80f2de78efb1fc8a4d0a187150df27c3b35d", "source_text": "An ordinal <MATH_0001> is called a <EMPHOPEN_0001>successor ordinal<EMPHCLOSE_0001> if there exists an ordinal <MATH_0002> such that <MATH_0003>. The smallest ordinal is <MATH_0004> which is also denoted <MATH_0005>. If <MATH_0006> is not <MATH_0007>, and not a successor ordinal, then <MATH_0008> is called a <EMPHOPEN_0002>limit ordinal<EMPHCLOSE_0002> and we have <MATH_0009>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:df6569a9f0bca8b61b83407eb97be22f304fd638607adc3a624d861b4343c1fd", "unit_id": "tag:05N1:p002"}
{"chapter": "sets", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "05N1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\omega$", "MATH_0002": "$\\omega_1$", "MATH_0003": "$\\in$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": " "}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7b5dc0a71137a4a2c925843041bda91fb0de3bf29106f7ef49b238cfe53b20a9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:23c32181e300762913be27fcb0ffc8f7c0fb6d075f57ac36f56e62e669a41aec", "source_text": "The first limit ordinal is <MATH_0001> and it is also the first infinite ordinal. The first uncountable ordinal <MATH_0002> is the set of all countable ordinals. The collection of all ordinals is a proper class. It is well-ordered by <MATH_0003> in the following sense: any nonempty set (or even class) of ordinals has a least element.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4aefb5120123684ce69973f2b1d500c26fbac5ddca1bc67ca9c3107f9eaffe4a", "unit_id": "tag:05N1:p003"}
